  "course_summary": "ISEN 620 | Survey of Optimization | Fall 2026\nInstructor: David Gutman | dhgutman@tamu.edu\nMeets: TR 3:55PM-5:10PM | ZACH 345\nGrading: Midterm I [25%], Midterm II [25%], Final Exam, Part I [25%], Final Exam, Part II [25%] — A: >90%, B: 80-89.99%, C: 70-79.99%, D: 60-69.99%, F: <60%\nTopics: K-K-T conditions, Lagrange conditions, Simplex Method, IP Algorithms, Graphical LP Solving, Sensitivity Analysis, IP Modeling, Networks, Classic Problems, deterministic linear optimization, deterministic nonlinear optimization, unconstrained-nonlinear optimization, constrained-nonlinear optimization, linear programming theory, nonlinear programming theory, linear programming algorithms, nonlinear programming algorithms, linear optimization models, nonlinear optimization models, small-scale optimization problems, large-scale problems, numerical algorithms, Basic Optimization Modeling, Non-linear Programming\nTools: Gurobi, optimization software\nPrerequisites: MATH 304 or MATH 311",
